Phasmid: generic font families (Windows profiles)

What:     A windows profile registers Windows Chrome's font pref defaults:
          Times New Roman, Arial, Consolas (fixed, as under ClearType),
          Comic Sans MS, Impact, Cambria Math, and the per-script entries of
          locale_settings_win.grd. The first of locale.languages selects
          Windows Chrome's ja, ko, zh-CN or zh-TW translations and the
          minimum logical font size. fonts.default_* still override the
          unknown-script entries. Linux profiles are unchanged.
Why:      A Linux build compiles only locale_settings_linux.grd, so monospace
          and math resolved to Linux family names Windows does not have.
Profile:  os.family, locale.languages, fonts.default_*
Hooks:    chrome/browser/ui/prefs/prefs_tab_helper.cc RegisterProfilePrefs
          (after fonts/availability.patch, whose PhasmidGenericFamily it
          reuses)
Contexts: main, iframes, workers.
Guard:    tests/guards/fonts/windows_metrics.py

